⭐ FINAL, CORRECT, SCALABLE ENGINE ARCHITECTURE

Canvas Class

Responsible for:

Creating DOM <canvas> or <svg>

Holding the list of shapes (this.shapes = [])

Creating the Engine

Creating the Renderer

Starting the engine automatically


class Canvas {
    constructor(config) {
        this.shapes = [];
        this.renderer = new Renderer(this);
        this.engine = new Engine(this.shapes, this.renderer);

        this.engine.start();  
    }

    addShape(shape) { this.shapes.push(shape); }
    removeShape(shape) { ... }
}

This matches your idea exactly.


+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++


⭐ Engine Class

Responsible for:

Running ONE global requestAnimationFrame loop

Updating all animations

Updating transforms

Marking dirty flags

Calling renderer once per frame


class Engine {
    constructor(shapes, renderer) {
        this.shapes = shapes;
        this.renderer = renderer;
        this.running = false;
    }

    start() {
        if (this.running) return;
        this.running = true;
        requestAnimationFrame(this.loop.bind(this));
    }

    loop(time) {
        // 1. Update animations
        for (const shape of this.shapes) {
            if (shape.animation) {
                shape.animation.update(time);  
            }
        }

        // 2. Render entire scene once
        this.renderer.render(this.shapes);

        // Continue loop
        requestAnimationFrame(this.loop.bind(this));
    }
}


+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++


⭐ Renderer Class

Renderer does ONLY drawing.

SVG Renderer:

Loops through shapes

Checks shape.dirty or similar something like that 

Updates only the changed DOM attributes

Never touches animation logic

Never touches state updates


Canvas Renderer:

Clears the canvas

Redraws all shapes in correct order

Shapes are already updated by the engine

No animation logic inside


+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++


⭐ Shape Class

Shape stores ONLY:

geometry

transform

styling

dirty flag

animation reference (just one pointer) or object 


Shape does NOT:

run rAF

call renderer

call animation itself

render itself

compute anything unrelated to data


+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++


⭐ Animation Class

Animation stored in shape:

shape.animation = new Animation(shape, options);

Animation stores:

precomputed frames or polynomial fit

duration

timing

easing

reference to shape

update(time) method 

all required data 


Animation NEVER calls rAF.
Animation NEVER calls renderer.

Engine calls:

shape.animation.update(time);

Animation updates shape.transform.
Shape marks dirty = true.

That’s it.


+++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++


⭐ “Whenever adding a shape, deleting a shape, applying transform, applying animation → everything happens automatically.”


Because the engine loop will always do:

UPDATE → RENDER → UPDATE → RENDER → ...

So ANY state change triggers correct rendering automatically.

We have a self-running scene graph.

